+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN BEHAVIOR -->
+### Behavior
+
+In confirmed MAIN standby, each fresh gas press of at least 0.1s and release requests one SET− press/release regardless of engagement or lateral activity. No extra release dwell or second press; actual stock ON stops remaining SET frames. Brake, CANCEL, MAIN OFF, renewed gas, driver buttons, lost eligibility or cancellation interrupt input. Cancellation takes priority.
+
+For new SET frames, compare the CAN receive-envelope timestamp with host dispatch time in the same boot-time clock and require newly observed CLU11 within 8ms; replay uses replay time. A buffered envelope cannot appear 0ms old merely because it is the latest CAN envelope; skip late samples without extending deadlines, adding a 10ms delay or remembering a timing phase. This age does not prove USB/wire completion or ECU acceptance.
+Skip a new sample when consecutive positive automatic requests at the actual host dispatch clock would be less than 15ms apart. Preserve ordinary approximately 19–20ms spacing, without replaying skipped samples later or extending press deadlines or frame budgets. Release and driver, brake or cancel interruptions do not wait for this spacing guard. This does not guarantee wire timing or ECU acceptance.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END BEHAVIOR -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN USAGE -->
+### Usage
+
+Turn the setting ON, update/restart while parked with MAIN OFF, then press MAIN ON after boot. Initial MAIN OFF is independent of AutoEngage. Each qualified release permits one press; another needs three seconds after the last TX and a fresh pedal cycle. Blocked/expired cues are not queued. OFF or an unauthorized profile sends no automatic SET; OFF preserves MAIN tracking.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END USAGE -->
+
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:BEGIN REFERENCE -->
+### Reference
+
+One press is at most six frames/120ms followed by release. The new Panda profile bounds one press to 120ms/six frames and ends its authorization on release, without a second press. Retain 0.5s MAIN settling, initial target/dashboard 30–160km/h and existing input/driver-priority guards. The current automatic-SET profile also requires front-left and rear-right wheel speeds at 30–160km/h. Discard releases below that wheel floor even if the dashboard exceeds 30; a fresh pedal cycle is required after speed recovers. `sample_age_ms` and `late_samples` report sample age and late-sample count. Absolute MAIN state is not decoded; standby already ON at restart needs a MAIN-OFF restart or actual stock ON from physical SET for synchronization. TX echo is not ECU acceptance; no direct braking, standstill launch or vehicle acceptance guarantee is provided.
+<!-- CARROT:SECTION:END REFERENCE -->
